AArch64 header-magic-publish-aarch64
(*
 * PUBLISH-BEFORE-WRITE on the hardware model. Same shape as
 * `grant-payload-publish-aarch64.litmus` but on the pair every segment in this
 * campaign depends on: a geometry field written first, then `magic` with a
 * RELEASE store; an attacher ACQUIRE-loads `magic` and only then reads the
 * geometry (`RunQuota-Shared-Memory-Structures.md` SS"Conventions Every Segment
 * Obeys").
 *
 * It is run separately rather than inferred from the payload pair because it is
 * the ordering three separate segment formats (lease, wait, ring) all rest on,
 * and because "structurally identical" is the kind of claim that is true until a
 * layout changes.
 *
 * RESULT (herd7 7.58, 2026-08-17): **FORBIDDEN / "Never"**.
 *)
{
0:X0=magic; 0:X1=budgetsOff;
1:X0=magic; 1:X1=budgetsOff;
}
 P0             | P1            ;
 MOV W2,#128    | LDAR W2,[X0]  ;
 STR W2,[X1]    | LDR W3,[X1]   ;
 MOV W3,#1      |               ;
 STLR W3,[X0]   |               ;
exists (1:X2=1 /\ 1:X3=0)
